     1,
     "<div>GGIR imputes missing data (non-wear) with the average of the same time point on other days of the recording, but if the accelerometer was also not worn on those other days for that time point it imputes zeros. Variable &quot;<span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">complete_24hcycle&quot; in the csv report should give a quick impression of whether this was the case.</span></span></span></span><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If you are interested in time series analysis without the help of GGIR then make sure you also export the non-wear detection to you understand where data was imputed. Note that the non-imputed epoch level data is available in the part 1 milestone data (folder: meta/basic)</span></span></span></span><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vincent</span></span></span></span><br></div><div><br></div><div>‐‐‐‐‐‐‐ Original Message ‐‐‐‐‐‐‐<br></div>"
